// An `is` whose type can never match the value's own, at every position: a warning, the test is
// false, and the arm it guards reads the value as `never` (the D16047 ruling, 2026-11-14).
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@PRELUDE@@
function __mk(k: i32): i32 { k + 1 }
// @@VALUE@@
__mk(4)
// @@TYPE@@
i32
// @@TEST@@
v is string
// @@HIT@@
print(0)
// @@MISS@@
print(42)
// @@WANT@@
42
